			"notes": "Refinements on top of the v1.8.0 strafe HUD rework.\n\n**HUD**\n- Centre marker (white 2×2 with a black plus-outline) replaces the vanilla crosshair, which is hidden while the strafe HUD is on.\n- Optimal markers are now the triangles' inner edges; triangle width scales inversely with FOV (Quake Pro = base width, half-FOV = double) so low FOV doesn't make them vanish.\n- Triangles hidden below 430 speed.\n- **Smooth motion**: velocity is interpolated between ticks by the frame's tick progress, so the whole HUD glides at your render framerate instead of snapping at 20 Hz.\n- Speed readout uses the bundled **Geo** font (white).\n\n**Config**\n- New **GUI** tab (Strafe HUD toggle moved here) with **Speed on XP bar**: shows your speed as the XP-bar level number (works even at 0 XP) and hides the HUD's own number.\n\n**Movement**\n- Walljump: a ceiling above you no longer registers as a wall you can jump off (embedded detection slices are ignored)."
		}
